lemmas.proof_markdown:
Apply the modal realization with a fixed $S\ge s$. Its global-to-local agreement ratio satisfies

$$
\frac{
\max_{\deg Q\le101}\operatorname{agr}(f,Q)
}{\epsilon}
<\frac{2/p}{r/(130p)}
=\frac{260}{r}
\longrightarrow0.
$$

Hence the antecedent holds for every fixed $c_0>0$ once $p$ is sufficiently large. On the other hand,

$$
\frac{\Gamma_s}{\epsilon^{s-\gamma}}
\le2^{s+2}(S-1)\epsilon^\gamma
\longrightarrow0,
$$

because $\epsilon\le26r/p\to0$. Thus the conclusion fails for every fixed $c_1>0$.

These counterexamples lie below every fixed target-range trigger. For each fixed $\eta>0$,

$$
\frac{\epsilon}{(101/p)^{1-\eta}}
=O_\eta\left(\frac{r}{p^\eta}\right)
\longrightarrow0.
$$

Accordingly, the counterexample does not refute an energy statement whose hypotheses are restricted to that target range.
